Title: Smooth Criminal
Artist: Michael Jackson
Key: A minor (Dorian)
Tempo: 118
Time: 4/4

# **Two chords to a bar.** The measured harmonic unit on this recording is two
# beats (bench/harmonic_rhythm.py, and `canon.harmonic_unit`), which is what every
# published chart of this song also says: `| Am G | F G |`, not `| Am | G | F | G |`.
# Writing it one chord a bar puts the whole chart at half the song's harmonic
# rhythm, and the resulting bar-count mismatch reads as a system defect.
#
# The owner's own failing case, on the exact video they ran: the 9:26 short film.
# Two things about that video shape the numbers.
#
# **The song does not start until about 1:07.** The first minute is dialogue over
# a room-tone bed, and the beat tracker emits **no beats at all** across a
# 51-second stretch of it — one gap in the grid, longer than most songs' intros.
# The bars here start where the music does, and the alignment is expected to gap
# through everything before that.
#
# **The harmony is a bass line, not a chord part.** There is no instrument
# sounding a third for most of the verse — Am, G and F are what the bass walks
# through under a single sustained A tonality — so a recognizer hearing Bm or C
# where the bass passes through B and C is hearing the recording correctly and
# charting it wrongly. That is the specific defect this entry exists to expose.

